; A signed zone with two children and a DS for neither of them, so both
; delegations are insecure and the denial of each DS is example.'s to
; make and to sign.
;
; up.example. is served by the other primary, so the delegation to it
; leads somewhere and is answered.  lame.example. names a server which
; is not there, which is the ordinary condition of an insecure
; delegation somebody has stopped looking after.
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 3600
@		IN	SOA	ns.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@		IN	NS	ns.example.
ns		IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
www		IN	A	192.0.2.1
up		IN	NS	ns.up.example.
ns.up		IN	A	{{ROOT_ADDR}}
lame		IN	NS	ns.lame.example.
ns.lame		IN	A	127.0.0.3
